# The impasto field is a cache: `poster` repaints it whenever the palette
# changes and it is several megabytes of pure derivation. The two-tone
# `pines-01-*` files next to it are not — they are the artwork `poster`
# actually consumes, and the ImageMagick invocation that made them is not
# recorded anywhere, so they are tracked.
share/art/processed/impasto-field.png
share/art/processed/impasto-field.json

# The clips the plate figure opens. Deliberately not tracked: no theme profile
# names them, `plates.js` just reads whatever is in the directory, so the rice
# works without them — and they are ~22MB of collected media that git would
# keep forever. The code and the click-point config *are* tracked; only the
# content is not. Drop clips back in ~/.local/share/rice/art/.plates/ and the
# figure picks them up.
share/art/.plates/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
